.Dd September 23, 2026
.Dt ICOWM-MENU 5
.Os IcoWM 1.0.1
.Sh NAME
.Nm menu.json
.Nd root desktop menu for IcoWM
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa menu.json
holds the entries of the menu that opens on a right click over the
empty desktop.
The file is optional: absent or unparseable, the menu still shows its
built-in footer, namely
.Ql Strutless/Strutted maximization ,
.Ql Rearrange windows ,
.Ql Reload configuration ,
.Ql Redraw all windows
and
.Ql Exit ,
with no separator before it.
.Pp
The file is a single object with one key,
.Ic menu ,
holding an array of entry objects.
Every entry has a
.Ic type ,
which is one of four:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql command
A clickable item that launches something.
It also needs
.Ic name ,
the label shown, and
.Ic command ,
what to run.
.It Ql submenu
A nested menu, revealed on hover or click.
It needs
.Ic name
and an
.Ic items
array of further entries.
.It Ql label
A heading that cannot be clicked.
It needs
.Ic name .
.It Ql separator
A dividing line, needing nothing else.
.El
.Pp
A
.Ic command
is expanded through
.Xr wordexp 3 ,
so
.Ql ~ ,
.Ql ${HOME}
and the like work.
Sub-shell command substitution is disabled.
Should the command fail to run,
.Xr icowm 1
logs a warning and shows an informational dialog, so nothing fails in
silence.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/icowm/menu.json
The file this page describes, at the first of the several locations
.Xr icowm 1
looks in.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A menu with a heading, two entries, a nested menu and a divider:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "menu": [
        { "type": "label", "name": "Applications" },
        { "type": "command", "name": "Terminal",
          "command": "xterm" },
        { "type": "command", "name": "Editor",
          "command": "gvim" },
        { "type": "separator" },
        {
            "type": "submenu",
            "name": "Utilities",
            "items": [
                { "type": "command", "name": "Files",
                  "command": "pcmanfm" },
                { "type": "command", "name": "Calculator",
                  "command": "xcalc" }
            ]
        }
    ]
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr icowm 1 ,
